{"objects":[{"id":"flow","instance":"instance--b96dad5f-c519-5a1f-a718-912ca4a86c02","objects":["attack-action--1","attack-action--2","attack-action--3","attack-action--4","attack-action--5","attack-action--6","attack-action--7","attack-condition--1","attack-condition--2","instance--763adce8-107c-58c1-9b65-18fefd501b17","instance--7797ff9e-6685-5e18-adfb-c4d44716e06f","software--2","instance--aaa15696-eba1-5630-abe7-6eeb65da1682","software--3","instance--becc7795-37fe-5653-834c-15b423ef23c9","instance--cd8e2e12-554c-5e0b-9908-bf5d0aaae299","instance--75bd3552-9387-5001-9510-8bba3a3bc0c6","instance--ca9ddeed-5dfe-54dd-9593-9e5889348c26","instance--3536a568-610f-5570-bba9-6dfe97bc9c2e","instance--384798bd-a84b-5feb-8d38-7f9d0a087f11","instance--057c9c6b-5f9d-5a42-a700-338d5f0eb74a","instance--7e8c9301-c3f8-55e9-8894-e81f1b6203d9","instance--b6d82c28-0a68-5c6f-b058-c1e072f51852","instance--365c3aa7-c8dc-5e18-93ce-f99f70d8e195","instance--5824580a-ff0f-5565-bba6-97a7c9ed3a5e","instance--1e3d4bfa-e0f8-5c07-9d99-9332bf484ae8","instance--c080a4ca-bd39-5747-b7cf-d95838e75c4f","instance--e5e1f9aa-9fe9-5106-95bc-0f29bb985397","instance--1fa3126a-bb58-563e-a616-464bda46b52f","instance--eebd1645-991e-522e-b90e-977b93c23a41","instance--458b9052-de4d-5b30-bc79-d8e8797debaf","instance--7381e3e7-e387-5414-8b46-0248ba18a3ff","instance--d67df2e3-f239-5084-b92d-d2446dc8f121","instance--399a759f-97f7-528c-90c7-de3363f46907","instance--6298e0ca-8198-59e9-b0c0-9ae0e17c9601","instance--b72a1620-7088-5849-909c-9fe36cf1e92b"],"properties":[["name","Working with a DB in a VPC"],["description","Procedural steps for creating and configuring an Amazon RDS DB instance in a VPC, including dual-stack mode and public accessibility prerequisites."],["scope","incident"],["author",[["name","Unknown"]]],["external_references",[["item-1",[["source_name","docs.aws.amazon.com"],["url","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonRDS/latest/UserGuide/USER_VPC.WorkingWithRDSInstanceinaVPC.html"]]]]]]},{"anchors":{"0":"instance--ad592d05-6969-5b51-98a8-1ad9b6aab896","120":"instance--5850a8f4-8241-5e73-9bf0-dcd376cd5025","150":"instance--0da1498f-3beb-5916-a249-e0410a4a81e4","180":"instance--d3632784-7391-5a29-83e2-edab51db56c6","210":"instance--8bc47ca5-ca73-5a04-a9ea-918608f10871","240":"instance--6546eef6-c5ad-516e-a417-89916e651648","270":"instance--244e5a69-f465-564e-9d2c-93d4da44fc57","30":"instance--6a1fca3c-fdb6-536a-bbea-61ac2349a700","300":"instance--043a5b44-2864-5565-abce-1909204e5485","330":"instance--e10eb918-2b0b-56f4-9c82-f345ce21276c","60":"instance--33a99d1b-dad8-51f6-be74-e1614db9151b","90":"instance--380c79e9-b1eb-547c-bf01-a011db1201c1"},"id":"action","instance":"attack-action--1","properties":[["name","Create VPC"],["description","Step 1: Create a VPC\n\nCreate a VPC with subnets in at least two Availability Zones. You use these\n\t\t\t\t\tsubnets when you create a DB subnet group. If you have a default VPC, a subnet\n\t\t\t\t\tis automatically created for you in each Availability Zone in the\n\t\t\t\t\tAWS Region."],["confidence",0.0],["ttp",{"tactic":"TA0042","technique":"T1583"}]]},{"anchors":{"0":"instance--4f4d03a8-4502-5010-997b-9943e254395b","120":"instance--cefe62ac-5b6e-5ead-84fc-b4c632913a73","150":"instance--4d07a740-2467-5b95-ac8d-4a2ee8edd11e","180":"instance--1205f03c-a457-5a0b-87ef-3bbb7aac110f","210":"instance--96e7dc6a-9f86-5f69-8d45-a566303cd4c0","240":"instance--66237af6-bb19-5a51-9fa2-cbc4a96186f5","270":"instance--836dfd42-b475-50ca-9acf-4f11bd32b89f","30":"instance--efe92997-cc5c-538a-90bc-c09ffb1379f4","300":"instance--9c4a24ae-1426-5cb5-9d7c-792e6dd325b7","330":"instance--06c6a74a-ca7d-5703-88ea-a06a0933d21a","60":"instance--5e4f84e5-56b7-5b8f-9bc3-b4d59d371123","90":"instance--019deb6a-bab3-57db-9a53-11e3564bf7a4"},"id":"action","instance":"attack-action--2","properties":[["name","Create DB subnet group"],["description","Step 2: Create a DB subnet group\n\nA DB subnet group is a collection of subnets (typically private) that you\n\t\t\t\t\tcreate for a VPC and that you then designate for your DB . A DB subnet group allows you to specify a particular VPC\n\t\t\t\t\twhen you create DB using the AWS CLI or RDS API. If you use\n\t\t\t\t\tthe console, you can just choose the VPC and subnets you want to use. Each DB\n\t\t\t\t\tsubnet group must have at least one subnet in at least two Availability Zones in\n\t\t\t\t\tthe AWS Region. As a best practice, each DB subnet group should have at least\n\t\t\t\t\tone subnet for every Availability Zone in the AWS Region."],["confidence",0.0],["ttp",{"tactic":"TA0005","technique":"T1578"}]]},{"anchors":{"0":"instance--0ce35aea-35a2-52ae-a67b-985306bdefe7","120":"instance--312639d5-e6d9-57b1-850d-28f0a1eac2f6","150":"instance--9551a25e-2558-512e-9894-dd64a8d662bf","180":"instance--403becce-e0ad-5dcd-bc14-7c00453907da","210":"instance--2305f501-2712-5ec6-9d4e-1371b011e937","240":"instance--cf1b8cf6-1cbd-5afb-b653-aa693889dab5","270":"instance--1d3dc59a-40a0-5670-aa3e-1304ff762003","30":"instance--77063d4f-503a-5e9b-b622-15aa2cc6a8e7","300":"instance--beaab67f-8a54-5982-8c5d-9d2ed2d42c9f","330":"instance--4d3274ff-ef14-5a53-99be-01575194a98e","60":"instance--4154a6bf-290b-5fce-a557-5dc0f3e700fb","90":"instance--2992bc0b-df57-54e5-a17b-03a964338c09"},"id":"action","instance":"attack-action--3","properties":[["name","Create VPC security group"],["description","Step 3: Create a VPC security group\n\nBefore you create your DB , you can\n\t\t\t\t\tcreate a VPC security group to associate with your DB . If you don't create a VPC security group, you can use the\n\t\t\t\t\tdefault security group when you create a DB ."],["confidence",0.0],["ttp",{"tactic":"TA0003","technique":"T1578.001"}]]},{"anchors":{"0":"instance--0f6e4da7-a5f4-54d7-866f-3bc6e8bcb019","120":"instance--015254b5-0906-577e-b3e3-3899f837d118","150":"instance--f7af5b8c-330a-58d5-b0da-a3d5f0bc6ad0","180":"instance--9f27ab21-2382-567d-b022-74ad5a29bd08","210":"instance--d799eb0a-7600-5b1a-a298-c47a78ceae4b","240":"instance--911c2c52-5974-5e08-b0b6-a9084d57c6ee","270":"instance--286444b4-97a1-58cd-9ca3-cffa04a15351","30":"instance--92192c38-5143-50e0-8c39-a96ea86e32e2","300":"instance--82bb3de0-bea5-5651-a1de-583283258c6d","330":"instance--4f0945c8-f644-50ce-8796-fea52a29dda1","60":"instance--16c43a2d-7356-521d-a507-5922e2c3337b","90":"instance--abce5c62-339a-5ed5-a0b8-dd66136cfe2f"},"id":"action","instance":"attack-action--4","properties":[["name","Enable VPC DNS attributes"],["description","If you want your DB in the VPC to be publicly\n\t\t\t\t\t\taccessible, you must enable the VPC attributes and ."],["confidence",0.0],["ttp",{"tactic":"TA0005","technique":"T1578"}]]},{"anchors":{"0":"instance--a469636c-0cb2-50b9-92f9-644c8aa98197","120":"instance--d57b3a21-e910-5879-8148-40165cea451a","150":"instance--58250ef4-5bb4-5bf3-b33e-89493bbb395d","180":"instance--3e769cf2-c1e5-5d2e-81d4-892f48ce4d86","210":"instance--f6499e41-749c-5d7f-9346-96c08d0d5dfd","240":"instance--d9dcdfc8-5f42-546a-803a-0efcd5d4cf91","270":"instance--c9afd0f6-97ce-57b2-9d60-3557b6214809","30":"instance--75f82155-f5ff-5619-8bf8-aae22937cab0","300":"instance--25e2d26e-1b35-56bd-b9aa-096c2d3b0e3c","330":"instance--e0483688-da10-5376-8cf2-050bcc3b70f0","60":"instance--1293d9cc-16b2-5c67-a453-bd144aab133a","90":"instance--2b43cd52-10db-5b15-8ad5-c4b59496528b"},"id":"action","instance":"attack-action--5","properties":[["name","Create DB instance in VPC"],["description","Step 4: Create a DB instance in the VPC\n\nIn this step, you create a DB and use the\n\t\t\t\t\tVPC name, the DB subnet group, and the VPC security group you created in the\n\t\t\t\t\tprevious steps.\n\nFor details on how to create a DB , see .\n\nWhen prompted in the section, enter the VPC\n\t\t\t\t\tname, the DB subnet group, and the VPC security group."],["confidence",0.0],["ttp",{"tactic":"TA0003","technique":"T1578.001"}]]},{"anchors":{"0":"instance--54fc1f38-f4e3-523e-b07c-73889b0d8df7","120":"instance--9cf45948-7040-5d7a-a1d5-3cb4d